# powder.env: every setting powder reads, grouped.
# sudo bin/install.sh creates /opt/apps/powder.env from this file (mode 0600)
# and fills the REQUIRED values. By hand instead:
#   cp docker/powder.env.example /opt/apps/powder.env && chmod 600 /opt/apps/powder.env
# then replace every CHANGE_ME and fill the REQUIRED values. Optional keys are
# commented out; powder runs without them.
# Docs: apps/web/content/docs/self-hosting.md

# ── runtime (set by the image; leave as is) ─────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=production
NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1
PORT=3000
HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0

# ── REQUIRED: database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The bundled postgres service in docker-compose.yml creates this database from
# POWDER_DB_*. DATABASE_URL, these three and POWDER_DB_PSQL (bin/self-deploy.sh)
# must name the same user and database. With NODE_ENV=production powder refuses
# to start while POWDER_DB_PASSWORD or DATABASE_URL still contain CHANGE_ME.
# Generate the password:  openssl rand -hex 24
POWDER_DB_USER=admin
POWDER_DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
POWDER_DB_NAME=powder
DATABASE_URL=postgres://admin:CHANGE_ME@powder-postgres:5432/powder
# DB network layout. Default: the DB is powder-postgres on the private powder-db
# network, reachable only by powder + worker. A server where it runs as `postgres`
# on the shared `internal` network (the shared-network layout) is detected by
# bin/self-deploy.sh, kept (docker-compose.shared-db.yml) and warned about. shared = keep the shared-network
# layout on purpose; private = move such a server (docs/SELF-HOSTING.md "DB
# network cutover").
# POWDER_DB_NETWORK=shared
# Container hardening (true|false). Default on: powder and worker run with
# cap_drop ALL + no-new-privileges (docker-compose.yml). false = opt out
# (bin/self-deploy.sh adds docker-compose.unharden.yml).
# POWDER_HARDEN=false
# Read-only web root filesystem (true|false, default false;
# docker-compose.web-readonly.yml):
# POWDER_WEB_READONLY=true

# ── REQUIRED: secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session signing and OAuth-token encryption.   Generate:  openssl rand -hex 32
# powder refuses to start with one shorter than 32 characters or low-entropy.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# AES-256-GCM key (64 hex chars) for deploy keys, webhook secrets and env vars.
# A patterned key (0000..., abab...) is refused as low-entropy.
# Generate:  openssl rand -hex 32   Keep a copy: losing it orphans every stored secret.
POWDER_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── REQUIRED: login ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public origin of the dashboard, e.g. https://powder.example.com
# Use https (only http://localhost is accepted without a boot warning).
# powder refuses to start without it: webhook URLs and dashboard links use it.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=
# GitHub OAuth app (callback URL: <BETTER_AUTH_URL>/api/auth/callback/github)
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Admin user ids, comma separated. Leave empty on a fresh install: enter the
# one-time setup token from the powder log ("[first-run] setup token: <token>")
# at /setup, then the first GitHub login becomes admin and the log prints
# "[first-run] ... POWDER_ADMIN_USER_IDS=<id>". Persist it with
#   sudo bin/install.sh --set-admin <id>
# (writes it here and recreates both containers), or put it here by hand and run
# docker compose --env-file /opt/apps/powder.env up -d --force-recreate powder worker
# (a plain restart does not re-read this file).
POWDER_ADMIN_USER_IDS=

# ── SSH to the servers you manage ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Create the key once on this server:  ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N '' -f /root/.ssh/id_ed25519
# docker-compose.yml mounts it (and the .pub) at the same path in both containers.
SSH_KEY_PATH=/root/.ssh/id_ed25519
# off = do not pin remote host keys (not recommended).
# POWDER_SSH_HOSTKEY_MODE=off

# ── client IP for rate limits ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Header that carries the real client IP (login, webhook and MCP limiters).
# x-real-ip (default): powder's Traefik in front, it sets X-Real-IP from the TCP
#   peer, so a client cannot pick its own rate-limit bucket.
# cf-connecting-ip: behind Cloudflare. Only safe when the server accepts HTTP(S)
#   from Cloudflare's IP ranges alone (firewall origin lock); otherwise a client
#   can send its own cf-connecting-ip and get a fresh bucket per request. Put the
#   lock in the DOCKER-USER iptables chain or a cloud firewall: ufw does not filter
#   ports Docker publishes.
# x-forwarded-for: the right-most hop (another proxy in front).
POWDER_TRUSTED_IP_HEADER=x-real-ip

# ── security: app compose files, builds and the test gate ───────────────────
# Every default below is the safe one; each line documents the opt-out.
# Compose guard (docs/SECURITY-COMPOSE.md): unset = enforce, refuse an app compose
# that breaks the allow-list. warn = log findings and still refuse the
# high-severity ones when the config changed (for an existing install that is
# still collecting findings).
# POWDER_COMPOSE_GUARD=warn
# Exemptions, JSON keyed by <serverId>/<app> or <app>, values are rule codes:
# POWDER_COMPOSE_GUARD_EXEMPT={"my-server/my-app":["network_mode"]}
# Builds pass --pull (FROM / COPY --from never resolve to another app's local
# image). 0 = off, e.g. when Docker Hub's anonymous pull limits block builds.
# POWDER_BUILD_PULL=0
# Extra docker networks apps may join besides their own and web/internal/infra
# (comma-separated), e.g. a stack network several apps on one server share.
# POWDER_SHARED_NETWORKS=mystack_default
# Test-gate memory cap (e.g. 2g). Unset = uncapped.
# POWDER_TESTGATE_MEM=2g
# Directory on the managed servers for powder's generated compose overrides
# (docker-compose.powder.yml per app). Default /var/lib/powder/compose; leave it.
# POWDER_COMPOSE_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/powder/compose
# Container hardening and the DB network layout: see the database section above
# (POWDER_HARDEN, POWDER_WEB_READONLY, POWDER_DB_NETWORK). Host key pinning:
# POWDER_SSH_HOSTKEY_MODE (SSH section). Client IP for rate limits:
# POWDER_TRUSTED_IP_HEADER (above). Boot refuses a BETTER_AUTH_SECRET or
# POWDER_ENCRYPTION_KEY that is short or low-entropy.

# ── deploys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run deploys in the worker container (recommended). Accepts true, 1, yes or on.
POWDER_DEPLOY_WORKER=true
# Render app env vars from powder's database to the server at deploy time.
POWDER_ENV_VARS_DB_MODE=true
# Settle window for push deploys, every app without its own value: seconds (at most
# 1800) a push deploy waits so further pushes fold into it. 0 = off. Unset keeps the
# current install default (off unless set). Applied when powder starts.
# POWDER_DEPLOY_SETTLE_SECONDS=120
# off = disable the pre-swap candidate check for every app.
# POWDER_SWAP_CHECK=off
# Containers an ops hub may never roll back automatically (GET /api/internal/auto-rollback),
# comma list, on top of powder's own. Per app: the automatic rollback toggle on its Settings tab.
# POWDER_AUTO_ROLLBACK_NEVER=
# Concurrent builds on a dedicated builder host (default 2).
# POWDER_BUILD_SLOTS=2
# Cap (GB) on the BuildKit cache of a dedicated build host. After every builder
# phase powder prunes cache there by age until `docker buildx du` Total is under it.
# POWDER_BUILDER_CACHE_CAP_GB=30
# `off`: a dedicated builder's build that failed on the commit itself (a test, lint
# or type check step, a rejected lockfile, a TypeScript error) falls back to a local
# build like any other failure, instead of failing the deploy at step `build`.
# POWDER_BUILDER_APP_VERDICT=off
# Self-deploy through powder: the compose service name of powder itself, and
# the id of the server it runs on (required with POWDER_SELF_SERVICE: without it
# the self-deploy is refused), so a deploy of powder detaches the recreate.
# POWDER_SELF_SERVICE=powder
# POWDER_SELF_SERVER_ID=
# Container name of powder (default powder), the compose service of the deploy
# worker that is rebuilt with it (default worker), and powder's source dir on
# that server (default: POWDER_SRC). With a source dir set, only a compose project
# under its parent dir counts as powder's own.
# POWDER_SELF_CONTAINER=powder
# POWDER_SELF_WORKER_SERVICE=worker
# POWDER_SELF_SRC=/opt/apps/powder/src
# Extra app names /new and the adopt flows refuse, comma-separated, for your own
# services that keep /opt/apps/<name> or /opt/apps/<name>.env on a server. Each is
# trimmed and lowercased and must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,30}$; at most 64 are read.
# POWDER_RESERVED_APP_NAMES=
# Traefik file-provider directory on the managed servers.
# POWDER_TRAEFIK_DYNAMIC_DIR=/opt/infra/traefik/dynamic
# off = no better-auth sign-in probe in the swap-check for any app (per app:
# POWDER_AUTH_CHECK in the app's env). Unset = on.
# POWDER_SWAP_CHECK_AUTH=off
# Postgres client image for backups (pg_dump) and the database size probe.
# Default: postgres:17-alpine pinned by digest (lib/tool-images.ts). Another
# value must be pinned too (name:tag@sha256:<64 hex>); an invalid one is ignored.
# POWDER_PG_TOOL_IMAGE=postgres:17-alpine@sha256:<64 hex>
# Regex (whole key, case-sensitive) of extra app env keys an API token may write
# or delete. Empty (default): a token may only write credential-shaped keys; the
# other deny rules still apply. Admin browser sessions may write any key.
# POWDER_TOKEN_ENV_ALLOW=FEATURE_[A-Z_]+

# ── compose-time (read by docker-compose.yml and bin/self-deploy.sh) ────────
# Path of this file (default /opt/apps/powder.env). docker-compose.yml,
# bin/install.sh and bin/self-deploy.sh read it from the shell environment. If
# the file lives elsewhere, set it here too (bin/install.sh does): powder then
# never renders an app's env file over it. Keep it outside the paths an app owns
# (/opt/apps/<name>.env, /opt/apps/<name>/); bin/install.sh refuses those.
# POWDER_ENV_FILE=/opt/apps/powder.env
# none = bin/install.sh sets up no Traefik and no POWDER_DASHBOARD_HOST (what
# --no-proxy writes here; --proxy overrides it for one run). Unset = Traefik.
# POWDER_PROXY=none
# File with the secret part of powder's own BuildKit cache ids, created once.
# Only bin/install.sh reads this variable (shell environment, not this file);
# bin/self-deploy.sh and the in-app self-deploy always use the default path.
# POWDER_BUILD_CACHE_ID_FILE=/opt/apps/.powder-build-cache-id
# Host port the dashboard listens on (127.0.0.1 only). Default 3050.
# POWDER_PORT=3050
# Parent directory of the postgres data dir (<dir>/powder-pgdata). Default /opt/apps.
# POWDER_DATA_DIR=/opt/apps
# Public hostname of the dashboard: adds a Traefik router (needs Traefik with a
# "le" cert resolver on the "web" network). Unset = no labels; front it yourself.
# POWDER_DASHBOARD_HOST=powder.example.com
# POWDER_DASHBOARD_HOST_ALIAS=www.powder.example.com
# POWDER_DASHBOARD_HOST_ALIAS2=
#
# Optional host split: public site + docs on one host, dashboard on another.
# Comma-separated public-site hosts. On them powder serves only the landing
# page, /docs, assets, /api/webhooks/*, /api/health and /ingest; everything
# else is a plain 404. The dashboard origin is BETTER_AUTH_URL. Route both
# through Traefik with the aliases above, e.g.
#   POWDER_DASHBOARD_HOST=deploy.example.com
#   POWDER_DASHBOARD_HOST_ALIAS=example.com
#   POWDER_DASHBOARD_HOST_ALIAS2=www.example.com
#   BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://deploy.example.com
#   POWDER_SITE_HOST=example.com,www.example.com
# New push webhooks use the first site host. Unset = no split, one host serves all.
# POWDER_SITE_HOST=

# ── schema on boot ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The powder container applies pending `-- idempotent` migrations before it
# serves (same rules as bin/self-deploy.sh, see apps/web/content/docs/upgrading.md).
# off = skip (bin/self-deploy.sh still applies them).
# POWDER_MIGRATE_ON_BOOT=off
# 1 = create the whole schema in an empty database. Without it an empty database
# (empty ledger, none of powder's tables) is refused, because a wrong DATABASE_URL
# or a moved data dir looks the same. bin/install.sh sets it on a new server and
# removes it once the schema exists; existing installs never need it.
# POWDER_ALLOW_FRESH_SCHEMA=1
# 1 = record the migration files that lack the -- idempotent marker (the list
# pinned in bin/lib-migrations.sh) as applied on this boot. Only for the first
# boot of a database whose schema was applied by hand; remove it afterwards.
# Ignored on an empty database.
# POWDER_MIGRATE_BASELINE=1
# Seconds the post-deploy migrations wait for /api/health before they are left
# for the next start (default 600).
# POWDER_MIGRATE_POST_WAIT=600
# Seconds the worker waits at start for powder to apply the pre-deploy
# migrations of its image (the migration ledger) before it starts anyway, with a
# warning naming the missing files (default 600).
# POWDER_WORKER_MIGRATION_WAIT=600

# ── backups (per-app postgres to S3-compatible storage) ─────────────────────
# All five must be set or the backup tick silently skips.
# BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.example.com
# BACKUP_S3_REGION=us-east-1
# BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=powder-backups
# BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Passphrase that encrypts dumps client-side.  Generate:  openssl rand -hex 32
# LOSING THIS MEANS LOSING THE BACKUPS.
# POWDER_BACKUP_KEY=
# Retention floor per app for scheduled backups (default 7).
# BACKUP_KEEP_PER_APP=7
# Retention floor per app for manual backups, a separate pool (default 3).
# BACKUP_KEEP_MANUAL_PER_APP=3
# 1 = an API token may delete backups (prune with dryRun:false), e.g. an ops hub
# that prunes on a schedule. Unset = only an admin browser session may.
# POWDER_TOKEN_BACKUP_PRUNE=1

# ── notifications ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JSON POST {event, app, server, message, url, at} for deploy_failed, app_down,
# app_up and cron_failed. Discord and Slack incoming webhooks work. Off when unset.
# POWDER_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=
# More webhooks and email targets: /settings/notifications. Email needs both:
# POWDER_SMTP_URL=smtps://user:pass@smtp.example.com:465
# POWDER_MAIL_FROM=Powder <alerts@example.com>

# ── "diagnose with AI" on failed CI runs ────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Max model calls per UTC day (default 50, 0 = off).
# POWDER_LLM_DAILY_MAX=50

# ── optional: ops endpoint reporting (nothing is sent unless the token AND a URL are set)
# Only for an ops endpoint of your own that ingests powder's events. For
# normal alerting use POWDER_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL above.
# POWDER_HQ_INGEST_TOKEN=
# POWDER_HQ_INGEST_URL=
# POWDER_HQ_GENERIC_URL=
# POWDER_HQ_CRON_URL=
# Project name sent with the reported events (default "powder").
# POWDER_HQ_PROJECT=powder
# Deploy-setup warning cards (/docs/deploys#deploy-setup-warnings): "on" posts
# them; unset or "off" only logs "[stability] would warn: <key> <reason>".
# POWDER_STABILITY_CARDS=off

# ── updates and analytics ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# off = no daily GitHub release check.
# POWDER_UPDATE_CHECK=off
# PostHog (read at image build time; pass via this file or build args). The KEY needs
# the HOST (e.g. https://eu.i.posthog.com): without it analytics stays off.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_UI_HOST=
